module SampleInchRuler

@ Author = "Benjamin Boeck" @

@ WorkpieceGeometry :"MinEdge":{"X":0.0,"Y":0.0,"Z":-10.0},"MaxEdge":{"X":175.0,"Y":30.0,"Z":0.0}@

# SAMPLE: a real inch ruler - whole inches, halves, quarters, eighths and sixteenths.
#
# How an inch ruler is built
#   An inch ruler is not "major / medium / minor". The inch is halved again and again, and every level
#   has its own tick length:
#       level 0  whole inch   longest tick, big number      1  2  3 ...
#       level 1  1/2 inch     shorter tick, small number    1/2
#       level 2  1/4 inch     shorter again, small number   1/4  3/4
#       level 3  1/8 inch     shorter again, no number
#       level 4  1/16 inch    shortest tick, no number
#   NewFractionScale builds exactly this. levels=4 stops at sixteenths, levels=5 would add 1/32.
#   The tick lengths and depths of the levels are derived from the longest tick (tickLength,
#   tickDepth) - or give your own list with the tickStyles parameter.
#
# Two text sizes
#   The whole-inch numbers (unitLabel) and the fractions (fractionLabel) are separate texts. By default
#   the fractions are 60 percent as big as the numbers; a fraction is written without the whole number
#   (3/4, not 1 3/4) because the big number before it already says the inch.
#   fractionLabelLevel=2 labels the halves and quarters; 1 would label only the halves, 0 no fractions.
#
# Inch without conversion
#   AxisSystem::ImperialMeasuring switches the whole control to inch: from then on every position,
#   length and feed in the program is in inch (feed in inch/min) and the library needs no
#   conversion - 6 simply means 6 inch. AxisSystem::MetricMeasuring at the end switches back.
#   (The WorkpieceGeometry above is given in millimetres.)
#
# Calling program duties (the library never does these)
#   Select the tool, set Rpm and Feed, switch the spindle on and off. Use a graver / engraving
#   tool; adapt Rpm and Feed to your tool and material. Z = 0 is the surface of the part.

using Base
using ScaleEngraver
import AxisSystem

export program Main
    # --- machine setup: the caller's job -------------------------------------------------------
    AxisSystem::ImperialMeasuring
    Absolute
    Rpm = 13000
    Feed = 30
    Spindle On

    # --- heights in inch -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # retractZ 0.08 = about 2 mm, approachZ 0.02 = about 0.5 mm above the surface, safeZ 0.8 inch
    heights = NewEngraveHeights(retractZ=0.08 approachZ=0.02 safeZ=0.8)

    # --- the numbers of the whole inches: 0.12 inch high; the 0 on the part edge is not written ----
    unitNumbers = NewLabelSettings(labelHeight=0.12 labelDepth=0.004 skipFirstLabel=true)

    # --- the ruler: starts at X=0.4 / Y=0.4 inch, 6 inch long, ticks point up (+Y), baseline engraved
    #     tickLength = longest tick (whole inch), shorter on every finer level; depth 0.008 inch
    inchRuler = NewFractionScale(
        originX=0.4
        originY=0.4
        scaleLength=6
        valueStart=0
        valueEnd=6
        unitLabel=unitNumbers
        levels=4
        tickLength=0.32
        tickDepth=0.008
        fractionLabelLevel=2
        baselineDepth=0.004
    )

    EngraveFractionScale scale=inchRuler heights=heights

    Spindle Off
    AxisSystem::MetricMeasuring
    MoveToParkPosition
endprogram

end
